{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '760,850p' bin/attavo; sed -n '1420,1545p' bin/attavo; sed -n '2440,2515p' bin/attavo; sed -n '1,230p' tests/test_doctor_sealed.py; sed -n '55,90p' tests/test_doctor.py; sed -n '80,110p' schema/manifest.schema.json; git show f2c4bc718bbd408edf7a1f4b500d7896edd8506b:attest/specs/158/spec.md | sed -n '1,220p'\"","aggregated_output":"    # Proposal, not yet ruled on (issue #54): a gate that retires nothing\n    # only adds, so proof one reports it here rather than waiting on the\n    # schema alone -- read_manifest never validates against the manifest\n    # schema at runtime, so a schema requirement is not an enforced one.\n    no_retires = [name for name, gate in sorted(gates.items()) if not gate.get(\"retires\")]\n    missing, accepted = [], []\n    for name, gate in sorted(gates.items()):\n        fixture = fixtures / name\n        if not fixture.is_dir():\n            missing.append(name)\n            continue\n        env = dict(os.environ)\n        item = fixture_item_id(fixture)\n        if item is not None:\n            env[\"ATTAVO_ITEM\"] = item\n        run = subprocess.run(gate[\"command\"], shell=True, cwd=str(fixture),\n                             capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, env=env)\n        if run.returncode == 0:\n            accepted.append(name)\n    if missing:\n        return p.fail(f\"gate(s) with no rejection fixture: {', '.join(missing)}\")\n    if accepted:\n        return p.fail(f\"gate(s) that accepted their rejection fixture: {', '.join(accepted)}\")\n    if no_retires:\n        return p.fail(f\"gate(s) with no retires: {', '.join(no_retires)}\")\n    return p.hold(f\"{len(gates)} gate(s) rejected their fixture\")\n\n\ndef _merges_reachable(root: Path) -> tuple[list[dict], str | None]:\n    \"\"\"(merges, refusal): every merge commit on the default branch's own\n    first-parent line -- sha, parents, and its own first-parent diff --\n    read by one process rather than the git log plus one git diff per\n    merge merge_introducing_records used to pay walking toward the one\n    it wants (issue #153). refs/remotes/origin/HEAD names the default\n    branch without hard-coding \"main\", the same primitive\n    diff_since_approval already uses (issue #52); walking from it rather\n    than from HEAD is what keeps a transport merge on an item branch, a\n    pull_request checkout's own synthetic test merge, and a merge_group's\n    temporary merge from ever being mistaken for an item's merge (issue\n    #169) -- none of those is reachable from the default branch's first-\n    parent line by definition. When refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is not set,\n    this refuses by name rather than guess, exactly as diff_since_approval\n    does.\n\n    The walk starts at HEAD itself when the current checkout is literally\n    on the branch refs/remotes/origin/HEAD names (an ordinary checkout of\n    the default branch, on push or on a developer's own machine) and at\n    the remote-tracking ref's own value otherwise (any other branch, or\n    the detached HEAD a pull_request or merge_group checkout leaves\n    behind) -- HEAD only ever *is* the default branch's first-parent line\n    in the former case; in the latter, only the remote-tracking ref names\n    it. --diff-merges=first-parent gives each merge's diff against its\n    first parent in the same pass git log --merges already makes to list\n    them, in the same order, newest first.\"\"\"\n    symref = subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"symbolic-ref\", \"-q\", \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\"],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    if symref.returncode != 0:\n        return [], \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is not set; run `git remote set-head origin -a`\"\n    default_remote_ref = symref.stdout.strip()\n    default_branch = default_remote_ref.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1]\n    current_branch = subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"symbolic-ref\", \"-q\", \"--short\", \"HEAD\"],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    default_ref = (\"HEAD\" if current_branch.returncode == 0\n                   and current_branch.stdout.strip() == default_branch\n                   else default_remote_ref)\n    try:\n        out = git(root, \"log\", default_ref, \"--first-parent\", \"--merges\",\n                 \"--diff-merges=first-parent\", \"--name-only\",\n                 \"--format=\\x01%H\\x1f%P\")\n    except RuntimeError:\n        return [], None\n    merges = []\n    for block in out.split(\"\\x01\")[1:]:\n        header, _, rest = block.partition(\"\\n\")\n        sha, parents = header.split(\"\\x1f\")\n        merges.append({\"sha\": sha, \"parents\": parents.split(),\n                       \"touched\": [line for line in rest.splitlines() if line.strip()]})\n    return merges, None\n\n\ndef merge_introducing_records(root: Path, records_rel: str, item: str,\n                              stages: tuple[str, ...],\n                              merges: list[dict] | None = None) -> tuple[str | None, str | None]:\n    \"\"\"(merge_sha, refusal): the merge commit on the default branch's own\n    first-parent line whose first-parent diff introduces a record for\n    every one of stages, under records_rel/item/ -- the same derivation\n    attest itself uses (derive_attest_items), read here so proof two\n    requires an item's stage records to have arrived by an actual merge\n    on the default branch, not merely to sit in the tree, and not by a\n            stop = gate_stop(rec.get(\"refusal\"))\n            cls, provenance = stop[\"class\"], stop[\"provenance\"]\n            if cls not in STOP_CLASSES:\n                problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.class {cls!r} names \"\n                                f\"no enumerated class\")\n                continue\n            if provenance not in STOP_PROVENANCES:\n                problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.provenance \"\n                                f\"{provenance!r} names no enumerated provenance\")\n                continue\n            if not stop.get(\"detail\"):\n                problems.append(f\"item {item_dir.name} {name} is a gate stop with no cause\")\n\n    older_note = f\"{older} record(s) before stop was recorded\"\n    if problems:\n        return p.fail(\"; \".join(problems), older_records=older)\n    return p.hold(f\"{checked} checked ({older_note})\" if checked == 0\n                 else f\"{checked} non-pass record(s) carry stop with a cause ({older_note})\",\n                 older_records=older)\n\n\ndef attestation_command(m: dict) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"[forge].attestation_command: the tenant's own read of the store,\n    given a merge sha on stdin, printing the statement as JSON on exit 0\n    and nothing on a non-zero exit. Absent is not passing (issue #158:\n    the doctor said done while #106, #148, #153 had no statement in the\n    store at all -- there was no key to read one through).\"\"\"\n    cmd = (m.get(\"forge\") or {}).get(\"attestation_command\")\n    return cmd if isinstance(cmd, str) and cmd.strip() else None\n\n\ndef statement_for(root: Path, cmd: str, merge_sha: str) -> tuple[dict | None, int]:\n    \"\"\"The statement the forge holds for merge_sha and the command's exit\n    code. The statement is None when the command exits non-zero or prints\n    anything but a JSON object -- exit 2 means the store itself could not\n    be read (issue #158, amended after build-05: distinct from exit 1,\n    the store read fine and simply held no statement).\"\"\"\n    run = subprocess.run(cmd, shell=True, cwd=str(root), input=merge_sha + \"\\n\",\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    if run.returncode != 0:\n        return None, run.returncode\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(run.stdout)\n    except ValueError:\n        return None, run.returncode\n    return (parsed if isinstance(parsed, dict) else None), run.returncode\n\n\ndef _is_ancestor(root: Path, earlier: str, later: str) -> bool:\n    run = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", earlier, later],\n                         capture_output=True, check=False)\n    return run.returncode == 0\n\n\ndef proof_every_attested_item_is_sealed(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\n    p = Proof(\"every-attested-item-is-sealed\", \"every attested item has its statement in the store\")\n    if m is None:\n        return p.fail(f\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no records directory is declared\")\n    cmd = attestation_command(m)\n    if cmd is None:\n        return p.fail(\"no [forge].attestation_command in the manifest; the store cannot be read\")\n    records_rel = m.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"records\", \"\")\n    records_dir = root / records_rel\n    if not records_dir.is_dir():\n        return p.fail(f\"no records directory under {records_dir}\")\n    items = load_records(records_dir)\n    complete = [item for item, stages in sorted(items.items()) if all(s in stages for s in STAGES)]\n\n    # [forge].sealed_since: merges at or before this sha predate the\n    # tenant's merge queue -- the self-tenant's own #106, #148, #153 were\n    # merged direct, with no merge_group run to seal them. They are\n    # named, never failed, the same window convention proof three keeps\n    # for commits before the manifest's own install.\n    since = (m.get(\"forge\") or {}).get(\"sealed_since\")\n    merges, refusal = _merges_reachable(root)\n    if refusal:\n        return p.fail(refusal)\n    sealed: list[str] = []\n    before_window: list[str] = []\n    unsealed: list[str] = []\n    not_merged: list[str] = []\n    not_read: list[str] = []\n    reasons: list[str] = []\n    for item in complete:\n        merge_sha, _ = merge_introducing_records(root, records_rel, item, STAGES, merges=merges)\n        if merge_sha is None:\n            not_merged.append(item)\n            continue\n        if isinstance(since, str) and since.strip() and _is_ancestor(root, merge_sha, since):\n            before_window.append(item)\n            continue\n        statement, exit_code = statement_for(root, cmd, merge_sha)\n        if statement is not None:\n            sealed.append(item)\n        elif exit_code == 2:\n            not_read.append(item)\n            reasons.append(f\"item {item} merged at {merge_sha[:12]}: not read -- \"\n                           f\"the store could not be read; {cmd!r} exited 2\")\n        else:\n            unsealed.append(item)\n            reasons.append(f\"item {item} merged at {merge_sha[:12]} has no statement in the store\")\n    if reasons:\n        return p.fail(\"; \".join(reasons), sealed=sealed, before_window=before_window,\n                      unsealed=unsealed, not_merged=not_merged, not_read=not_read)\n    return p.hold(f\"{len(sealed)} merged item(s) sealed, {len(before_window)} before the window, \"\n                 f\"{len(not_merged)} not merged\",\n                 sealed=sealed, before_window=before_window, unsealed=unsealed,\n                 not_merged=not_merged, not_read=not_read)\n\n\ndef doctor(root: Path) -> list[Proof]:\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    return [proof_every_gate_rejects(root, m),\n            proof_one_item_every_stage(root, m),\n            proof_no_commit_lacks_record(root, m),\n            proof_no_stop_lacks_cause(root, m),\n            proof_no_invocation_lacks_record(root, m),\n            proof_every_attested_item_is_sealed(root, m)]\n\n\ndef cmd_doctor(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    as_json = \"--json\" in argv\n    args = [a for a in argv if a != \"--json\"]\n    root = Path(args[0] if args else \".\").resolve()\n    proofs = doctor(root)\n    if as_json:\n    other than success/neutral/skipped, is not green.\"\"\"\n    run = subprocess.run(f\"{checks_command} {shlex.quote(sha)}\", shell=True, cwd=str(root),\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    conclusions = []\n    for line in run.stdout.splitlines():\n        line = line.strip()\n        if not line:\n            continue\n        parts = line.rsplit(\" \", 1)\n        if len(parts) == 2:\n            conclusions.append({\"name\": parts[0], \"conclusion\": parts[1]})\n    # A commit the forge has no record of is not green -- it is unread.\n    # The executor's own commit is exactly this: the forge attaches\n    # checks to a pull request's head, and that commit stops being the\n    # head the moment a record commit lands on top of it. all() over an\n    # empty list is True, which is why this is spelled out rather than\n    # implied by the loop above.\n    ok = run.returncode == 0 and bool(conclusions) and all(\n        c[\"conclusion\"] in FORGE_OK_CONCLUSIONS for c in conclusions)\n    return {\"command\": checks_command, \"sha\": sha, \"conclusions\": conclusions}, ok\n\n\ndef diff_since_approval(root: Path, approval_sha: str | None) -> tuple[str, str | None]:\n    \"\"\"(diff_text, refusal): the item's own work since approval, not\n    everything merged onto the branch since then (issue #52) -- a\n    three-dot diff against approval_sha itself is not enough, since\n    approval_sha is already an ancestor of HEAD in the normal flow and\n    merge-base(approval_sha, HEAD) is just approval_sha again (verified\n    empirically, see issue #52). Diffing from the merge-base of HEAD and\n    the remote's default branch instead excludes content that arrived by\n    merging that branch in, because that content is already present on\n    both sides of the merge base. refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is what names\n    the default branch without hard-coding \"main\"; when it is not set,\n    there is nothing to diff against and this refuses rather than guess.\n    (\"\", None) when approval_sha is falsy -- nothing to diff from at all.\n    Shared by cmd_verify and cmd_counsel, which both hand an adapter this\n    same diff.\"\"\"\n    if not approval_sha:\n        return \"\", None\n    symref = subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"symbolic-ref\", \"-q\", \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\"],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    if symref.returncode != 0:\n        return \"\", \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is not set; run `git remote set-head origin -a`\"\n    diff_base = git(root, \"merge-base\", symref.stdout.strip(), \"HEAD\").strip()\n    return git(root, \"diff\", diff_base, \"HEAD\"), None\n\n\ndef cmd_verify(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    item_id = argv[0] if argv else derive_item_id(root)\n    if not item_id:\n        print(\"attavo verify: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo verify: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    specs_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"specs\"]\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    item_records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n\n    latest_build = latest_record(item_records_dir, \"build\")\n    if latest_build is None:\n        print(f\"attavo verify: refused: no build record for item {item_id}\")\n        return 1\n    if latest_build.get(\"status\") != \"pass\":\n        print(f\"attavo verify: refused: latest build record is \"\n              f\"{latest_build.get('status')!r}, not pass\")\n        return 1\n\n    forge_cfg = m.get(\"forge\") or {}\n    checks_command = forge_cfg.get(\"checks_command\")\n    if not checks_command:\n\"\"\"The doctor's fifth proof: every attested item has its statement in the\nstore (issue #158). This repository's own #106, #148, #153 were merged\ndirect, with no merge_group run and so no statement, and the doctor said\ndone anyway -- proof two held on the four stage records with the chain\nheld, never asking whether the merge was sealed.\n\nRun: python3 -m pytest tests -q\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nATTAVO = ROOT / \"bin\" / \"attavo\"\n\nFAKE_ATTEST = (\n    '#!/bin/sh\\nread sha\\ngrep -qx \"$sha\" sealed.txt && printf %s '\n    '\"{\\\\\"_type\\\\\": \\\\\"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1\\\\\"}\"\\n'\n)\n\n\ndef _git(root: Path, *args: str) -> str:\n    return subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), *args], capture_output=True, text=True,\n                          check=True).stdout.strip()\n\n\ndef _tenant_with_two_merged_items(tmp_path: Path) -> tuple[Path, str, str]:\n    root = tmp_path / \"sealed\"\n    root.mkdir()\n    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"init\", \"-q\", \"-b\", \"main\", \".\"], cwd=root, check=True)\n    _git(root, \"config\", \"user.email\", \"doctor@attavo.invalid\")\n    _git(root, \"config\", \"user.name\", \"doctor fixture\")\n    (root / \"attavo.toml\").write_text(\n        '[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n\\n[forge]\\nattestation_command = \"sh ./fake-attest\"\\n')\n    (root / \"fake-attest\").write_text(FAKE_ATTEST)\n    (root / \"sealed.txt\").write_text(\"\")\n    _git(root, \"add\", \".\")\n    _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"install\")\n    merges = []\n    for item in (\"1\", \"2\"):\n        _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"-b\", f\"attavo/{item}-x\")\n        (root / \"records\" / item).mkdir(parents=True)\n        for stage in (\"spec\", \"approval\", \"build\", \"verify\"):\n            (root / \"records\" / item / f\"{stage}-01.json\").write_text('{\"status\": \"pass\"}')\n            _git(root, \"add\", \"records\")\n            _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", f\"{stage} record for item {item}\")\n        _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"main\")\n        _git(root, \"merge\", \"-q\", \"--no-ff\", \"-m\", f\"Merge branch 'attavo/{item}-x'\", f\"attavo/{item}-x\")\n        merges.append(_git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"))\n    _git(root, \"update-ref\", \"refs/remotes/origin/main\", _git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"main\"))\n    _git(root, \"symbolic-ref\", \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\", \"refs/remotes/origin/main\")\n    return root, merges[0], merges[1]\n\n\ndef _tenant_with_one_merged_and_one_unmerged_item(tmp_path: Path) -> Path:\n    root = tmp_path / \"unmerged\"\n    root.mkdir()\n    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"init\", \"-q\", \"-b\", \"main\", \".\"], cwd=root, check=True)\n    _git(root, \"config\", \"user.email\", \"doctor@attavo.invalid\")\n    _git(root, \"config\", \"user.name\", \"doctor fixture\")\n    (root / \"attavo.toml\").write_text(\n        '[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n\\n[forge]\\nattestation_command = \"sh ./fake-attest\"\\n')\n    (root / \"fake-attest\").write_text(FAKE_ATTEST)\n    (root / \"sealed.txt\").write_text(\"\")\n    _git(root, \"add\", \".\")\n    _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"install\")\n    _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"-b\", \"attavo/1-x\")\n    (root / \"records\" / \"1\").mkdir(parents=True)\n    for stage in (\"spec\", \"approval\", \"build\", \"verify\"):\n        (root / \"records\" / \"1\" / f\"{stage}-01.json\").write_text('{\"status\": \"pass\"}')\n        _git(root, \"add\", \"records\")\n        _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", f\"{stage} record for item 1\")\n    _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"main\")\n    _git(root, \"merge\", \"-q\", \"--no-ff\", \"-m\", \"Merge branch 'attavo/1-x'\", \"attavo/1-x\")\n    m1 = _git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\n    (root / \"sealed.txt\").write_text(m1 + \"\\n\")\n    _git(root, \"add\", \"sealed.txt\")\n    _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"seal item 1\")\n    _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"-b\", \"attavo/2-x\")\n    (root / \"records\" / \"2\").mkdir(parents=True)\n    for stage in (\"spec\", \"approval\", \"build\", \"verify\"):\n        (root / \"records\" / \"2\" / f\"{stage}-01.json\").write_text('{\"status\": \"pass\"}')\n        _git(root, \"add\", \"records\")\n        _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", f\"{stage} record for item 2\")\n    _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"--detach\")\n    _git(root, \"merge\", \"-q\", \"--no-ff\", \"-m\", \"synthetic test merge of attavo/2-x into main\", \"main\")\n    return root\n\n\ndef _proof(root: Path) -> dict:\n    run = subprocess.run([\"python3\", str(ATTAVO), \"doctor\", \"--json\", str(root)],\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    proofs = json.loads(run.stdout)[\"proofs\"]\n    return [p for p in proofs if p[\"proof\"] == \"every-attested-item-is-sealed\"][0]\n\n\ndef test_doctor_proof_six_fails_on_an_unsealed_merge(tmp_path):\n    root, m1, m2 = _tenant_with_two_merged_items(tmp_path)\n    (root / \"sealed.txt\").write_text(m1 + \"\\n\")\n    p = _proof(root)\n    assert not p[\"holds\"]\n    assert \"item 2\" in p[\"reason\"] and m2[:12] in p[\"reason\"]\n    assert p[\"sealed\"] == [\"1\"] and p[\"unsealed\"] == [\"2\"]\n\n\ndef test_doctor_proof_six_holds_when_every_merge_is_sealed(tmp_path):\n    root, m1, m2 = _tenant_with_two_merged_items(tmp_path)\n    (root / \"sealed.txt\").write_text(m1 + \"\\n\" + m2 + \"\\n\")\n    p = _proof(root)\n    assert p[\"holds\"] and p[\"sealed\"] == [\"1\", \"2\"]\n\n\ndef test_doctor_proof_six_names_a_merge_before_the_window_without_failing(tmp_path):\n    root, m1, m2 = _tenant_with_two_merged_items(tmp_path)\n    (root / \"sealed.txt\").write_text(m2 + \"\\n\")\n    (root / \"attavo.toml\").write_text(\n        '[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n\\n[forge]\\nattestation_command = \"sh ./fake-attest\"\\n'\n        f'sealed_since = \"{m1}\"\\n')\n    p = _proof(root)\n    assert p[\"holds\"] and p[\"before_window\"] == [\"1\"] and p[\"sealed\"] == [\"2\"]\n\n\ndef test_doctor_proof_six_fails_without_an_attestation_command(tmp_path):\n    root = tmp_path / \"bare\"\n    root.mkdir()\n    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"init\", \"-q\", \"-b\", \"main\", \".\"], cwd=root, check=True)\n    (root / \"attavo.toml\").write_text('[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n')\n    (root / \"records\").mkdir()\n    p = _proof(root)\n    assert not p[\"holds\"] and \"attestation_command\" in p[\"reason\"]\n\n\ndef test_doctor_proof_six_says_not_read_when_the_store_cannot_be_read(tmp_path):\n    root = tmp_path / \"unreadable\"\n    root.mkdir()\n    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"init\", \"-q\", \"-b\", \"main\", \".\"], cwd=root, check=True)\n    _git(root, \"config\", \"user.email\", \"doctor@attavo.invalid\")\n    _git(root, \"config\", \"user.name\", \"doctor fixture\")\n    (root / \"attavo.toml\").write_text(\n        '[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n\\n[forge]\\nattestation_command = \"sh ./unreadable-store\"\\n')\n    (root / \"unreadable-store\").write_text(\n        '#!/bin/sh\\nread sha\\necho \"gh: not logged in\" >&2\\nexit 2\\n')\n    _git(root, \"add\", \".\")\n    _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"install\")\n    _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"-b\", \"attavo/1-x\")\n    (root / \"records\" / \"1\").mkdir(parents=True)\n    for stage in (\"spec\", \"approval\", \"build\", \"verify\"):\n        (root / \"records\" / \"1\" / f\"{stage}-01.json\").write_text('{\"status\": \"pass\"}')\n        _git(root, \"add\", \"records\")\n        _git(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", f\"{stage} record for item 1\")\n    _git(root, \"checkout\", \"-q\", \"main\")\n    _git(root, \"merge\", \"-q\", \"--no-ff\", \"-m\", \"Merge branch 'attavo/1-x'\", \"attavo/1-x\")\n    _git(root, \"update-ref\", \"refs/remotes/origin/main\", _git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"main\"))\n    _git(root, \"symbolic-ref\", \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\", \"refs/remotes/origin/main\")\n    p = _proof(root)\n    assert not p[\"holds\"]\n    assert \"not read\" in p[\"reason\"] and \"unreadable-store\" in p[\"reason\"] and \"exited 2\" in p[\"reason\"]\n    assert p[\"not_read\"] == [\"1\"] and p[\"unsealed\"] == [] and p[\"sealed\"] == []\n\n\ndef test_doctor_proof_six_names_an_unmerged_item(tmp_path):\n    root = _tenant_with_one_merged_and_one_unmerged_item(tmp_path)\n    noref = _proof(root)\n    assert not noref[\"holds\"] and \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\" in noref[\"reason\"]\n    _git(root, \"update-ref\", \"refs/remotes/origin/main\", \"main\")\n    _git(root, \"symbolic-ref\", \"refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\", \"refs/remotes/origin/main\")\n    ref = _proof(root)\n    assert ref[\"holds\"]\n    assert ref[\"sealed\"] == [\"1\"] and ref[\"not_merged\"] == [\"2\"] and ref[\"unsealed\"] == []\n\ndef test_no_stop_lacks_cause():\n    \"\"\"Proof 4, issue #94. Every non-pass build or verify record at\n    record_version 3 or later carries a stop naming its class and cause.\"\"\"\n    p = run_doctor(ROOT)[\"no-stop-lacks-cause\"]\n    assert p[\"holds\"], p[\"reason\"]\n\n\ndef test_no_invocation_lacks_record():\n    \"\"\"Proof 5, issue #151. Every <stage>-NN.started marker under\n    paths.records has arrived at its own <stage>-NN.json, or is still a\n    live process on this host.\"\"\"\n    p = run_doctor(ROOT)[\"no-invocation-lacks-record\"]\n    assert p[\"holds\"], p[\"reason\"]\n\n\ndef test_every_attested_item_is_sealed():\n    \"\"\"Proof 5, issue #158. Every merged, fully-staged item has a\n    statement in the forge's attestation store for its merge commit --\n    #106, #148, #153 predate [forge].sealed_since and are named before the\n    window instead.\"\"\"\n    p = run_doctor(ROOT)[\"every-attested-item-is-sealed\"]\n    assert p[\"holds\"], p[\"reason\"]\n\n\ndef test_record_loader_uses_highest_attempt_number(tmp_path):\n    \"\"\"Acceptance 2a. <stage>-NN.json files are one stage's attempts; the\n    doctor treats the highest NN as latest, and STAGES is unchanged.\n\n    spec-01.json names a commit that isn't on the branch at all; spec-02.json\n    names the real code commit. Proof 3 holds only if the loader reads\n    spec-02, not spec-01 -- i.e. only if it picks the highest attempt.\n    \"\"\"\n    root = tmp_path / \"attempts\"\n    root.mkdir()\n    (root / \"attavo.toml\").write_text('[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n')\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"checks_command\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Takes a full commit sha on argv; prints one line per check as \\\"<name> <conclusion>\\\". attavo verify runs it on the item's latest build record's sha before calling any adapter.\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"file_issue_command\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Reads one finding as JSON on stdin and files it as a tenant issue. attavo file-findings runs it once per finding in the item's latest verify record.\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"attestation_command\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Reads a merge commit sha on stdin and prints that merge's attestation statement as JSON on exit 0; nothing on a non-zero exit. The doctor's fifth proof runs it once per merged, fully-staged item to require a statement in the store.\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"sealed_since\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"A commit sha. A merge at or before it predates the tenant's merge queue and is named by the doctor's fifth proof as before the window rather than failed.\",\n          \"minLength\": 7\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"spec\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"required\": [\"boundary\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"boundary\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-cbKUjceg' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-3XEnldIC' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n## Problem\n\n`attavo doctor` reported done on this repository on 2026-09-17 while none of its three traversals (#106, #148, #153) had a statement in the attestation store: `main` had classic protection and no merge queue, every merge was direct, the coherence workflow's `merge_group` trigger never fired, and proof two holds on the four stage records with the chain held without asking whether the merge was sealed. The store answers 404 for all three; the operator screen rendered the missing statements as `not read`.\n\nRetires: the doctor's `done` on an unattested traversal; `not read` as the rendering of a statement that does not exist.\n\nAmended 2026-09-18 after #169 landed on `main` under this item's approved tree: an item's merge is the merge on the default branch's first-parent line (read from `refs/remotes/origin/HEAD`, refused by name when the ref is unset), so the proof names an item with no such merge in `not_merged` rather than skipping or failing it, fails by name on the walk's refusal, and the fixtures set the ref they depend on. The approval bound to the previous spec commit expires with this amendment, as the product requires.\n\nAmended again 2026-09-18 after build-05: the doctor job's pytest step ran `gh` with no token, the attestation command exited 2, and proof six called #151's sealed merge unsealed. Exit 2 from the command is \"the store could not be read\", a fact the proof now reports as `not read` by item, with the command and its exit in the reason, never as `unsealed`; and the doctor job carries `GH_TOKEN` at the job level so every step that runs the doctor can read the store. The approval expires again with this amendment.\n\n## Claims\n\n- bin/attavo\n- schema/manifest.schema.json\n- attavo.toml\n- .attavo/bin/forge-attestation\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml\n- tests/test_doctor_sealed.py\n- tests/test_doctor.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- doctor-fails-on-an-unsealed-merge.sh: on a fixture tenant with two merged items whose [forge].attestation_command answers for one merge and not the other, attavo doctor --json fails proof every-attested-item-is-sealed naming item 2 and its merge sha, listing sealed, unsealed, before_window, and not_merged, and holds once the command answers for both\n- doctor-fails-without-attestation-command.sh: a manifest with no [forge].attestation_command fails the proof naming the key, and the manifest schema declares the key\n- doctor-names-an-unmerged-item.sh: on a fixture tenant with one sealed merged item and a second item whose records sit on a branch under a synthetic merge at HEAD, the proof holds with sealed [\"1\"], not_merged [\"2\"], and unsealed []; before refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is set, the proof fails naming that ref\n- doctor-says-not-read-when-the-store-cannot-be-read.sh: on a fixture tenant with one merged item whose [forge].attestation_command exits 2, the proof fails with a reason containing \"not read\", the command, and \"exited 2\", with not_read [\"1\"], unsealed [], and sealed []\n- the-doctor-job-carries-the-token.sh: in .github/workflows/ci.yml the doctor job sets GH_TOKEN at the job level, declares attestations: read, and its pytest step over tests/test_doctor.py selects every_attested_item_is_sealed\n- the-proof-has-its-test.sh: tests named test_doctor_proof_six_fails_on_an_unsealed_merge, test_doctor_proof_six_names_an_unmerged_item, and test_doctor_proof_six_says_not_read_when_the_store_cannot_be_read exist under tests/, this repository's manifest names its attestation command, and .attavo/bin/forge-attestation is executable\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
